  "content": "## Opatija Safety: Key Advice\n\nOpatija maintains a very low crime rate. Your trip will likely be trouble-free.\n\n*   **Petty Theft**: Guard your valuables. Pickpocketing occurs, particularly in crowded market areas or popular tourist viewpoints. This is usually not worth the extra cost for "anti-theft" specific bags; common sense is sufficient.\n*   **Driving & Parking**: Roads are well-maintained. Parking can be challenging and expensive, especially during peak season. Never leave valuables visible in your parked vehicle.\n*   **Sea Safety**: Observe flag warnings at beaches. Strong currents can occur. Wear appropriate footwear; sea urchins are common on rocky shores.\n*   **Tourist Scams**: Be wary of overly friendly strangers offering unsolicited "help" or highly discounted tours. Always confirm prices upfront, especially with informal services.\n*   **Emergencies**: Dial 112 for all emergencies (Police, Ambulance, Fire). Emergency services are efficient and responsive.",
